 "notes": "Base-game pack. Encounter pools generated from PokéAPI data, merged to location level across sub-areas, encounter methods, and the paired versions (in-game trades and raid/event distributions excluded); area order is estimated from encounter levels and is approximate. No encounter tables are available from PokéAPI for this game — use custom areas in the encounter log to track catches. First-run teams only (postgame rematches with much higher levels are not included). Gym order and all teams/levels mirror Diamond & Pearl and were verified against BDSP-specific guides (Nintendo Life, Game8, RPG Site, GamerGuides, Attack of the Fanboy). One contested figure: Byron's Steelix is listed at Lv 35 by Attack of the Fanboy, but Lv 36 by Game8, GamerGuides, the GameFAQs BDSP FAQ and Diamond/Pearl parity -- 36 is used. BDSP's Elite Four famously use competitive movesets, held items, EVs and natures, but per this pack's format moves/abilities/items are left blank; the difficulty spike over the originals is in builds, not levels (e.g. Cynthia's Garchomp is Lv 66 as in D/P).",
